// TEST: Comm contradicts conjugating named function (rejects)
// ERROR: BL4013
// The named-function twin of symmetry/039: `where comm` on a declaration
// whose body deduces PConj rejects AT THE DECL, the same seam
// functions/030 pins for the PNeg case. The refusal is gated on the
// body's element type being provably complex at the declaration --
// annotated params make it so here; a generic declaration stays trusted
// at the decl (conj is the identity over reals), which is why the
// annotations below are load-bearing.
function hprod(a: Complex128, b: Complex128) where comm(a, b) = a * conj(b)
